# Version bump → commit → push

Whenever recognition/logic changes ship with a new **versionCode** / **versionName** bump in `app/build.gradle.kts`:

1. Finish the code change and bump the version (every testable build needs a distinguishable version).
2. **Commit and push to GitHub without waiting to be asked** — the user tests on device by pulling each version.

Commit message: one line on the fix + optional body with what to verify on Evaluate.

Do not skip push after commit. Do not bump version without committing unless the user explicitly says not to push yet.
